      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5d21c1a8154b187933d51a3e|full_name} I understand how this might seem like a non-issue considering the majority of canvas use-cases, but the issue is that this is a problem for those who explicitly rely on this not happening. It's frustrating to wake up one day and realize your VRChat world that relies entirely on pixel graphics has blurry canvases despite looking fine in the Unity editor.\n\nIf people want to disable anti-aliasing on canvases, they should be given the freedom to do so for whatever reason they see fit. Most people won't take advantage of this, and that's fine, but I wouldn't personally completely dismiss a bug report over it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
