      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6309625e2a885444c2180a28|full_name}: Yes, our client automatically replaces instances of the default Unity UI shader it finds with a supersampled version. This works in 99% of cases and results in a genuine improvement, but can have edge cases like this.\n\nThe SDK should now include an info box that notifies you of this replacement behaviour and offers to do the replacement in editor too. That way, the visual would match between editor and in-game.\n\nAs noted by @{5d21c1a8154b187933d51a3e|full_name} below this is very intentional and since there is no easy way to detect edge cases like this, the core ask here isn't really anything we can or will address.\n\nWith the above note on the SDK side, is there anything else we should do here or are you okay with closing this ticket?",
