  "details": "Pictured below: In game, pixel perfect images(Texture Type: Sprite(2D and UI, Filter Mode: Point (no filter) compression: None) on a canvas has anti-aliasing; it didn't use to look like this. The Unity Editor version shows closer to how it use to look; the image would use nearest pixel approximation and have no anti-aliasing effects. With this change, there is now no way to display pixel perfect images free of filtering (that I know of). Also, the lack of parity between how it looks in editor and in game can be a cause for concern. This also is not fixed by modifying my anti-aliasing modifier in the graphics settings.",
